SWARM 1a — SETTLEMENT QUARANTINE for the accuracy registry
==========================================================

TARGET FILE   tools/accuracy_registry.py   (the ONLY file this patch touches)
BASE          branch hmm-regime-and-pbo, HEAD 0b1f73b, file unmodified at HEAD

APPLY         from the repository root:
                  git apply --check round2-drafts/patches/grader-quarantine.patch
                  git apply         round2-drafts/patches/grader-quarantine.patch
REVERT            git apply -R      round2-drafts/patches/grader-quarantine.patch

WHAT IT DOES
  Excludes, from every directional tally and every reliability bin the registry
  publishes, any resolved prediction_outcomes row whose label was frozen BEFORE
  its forward bar's session had closed — i.e. the rows the resolver graded
  against a partial bar. The predicate is structural and per-row: it rebuilds
  the same base / target / forward bars PredictionResolver.Run selects
  (daemon/internal/pipeline/predict.go) and compares resolved_at against that
  forward bar's true session close (bar stamp + 16h for stocks, whose 1d bars
  are stamped at ET midnight; + 24h for crypto, stamped at UTC midnight).

  It does NOT use a timestamp cutoff and it does NOT touch basis_epoch.
  basis_epoch has zero readers in the daemon and zero in this grader, so
  stamping it excludes nothing from any published number. A ts cutoff is wrong
  for a different reason: the deployed binary (rev 0499416) has no settlement
  guard, so the contamination window is OPEN and a cutoff would silently stop
  excluding rows that are still being minted.

  Nothing is written and nothing is relabelled. Every row stays in
  prediction_outcomes exactly as frozen; only the tally changes.

SELF-DESCRIBING OUTPUT (required — a silent exclusion is as dishonest as a
silent inclusion)
  * console: a "Settlement quarantine:" block beside the survivorship boundary,
    giving rows excluded / considered, the split between mid-session freezes and
    unverifiable rows, the INDEPENDENT observations lost after dedup, a
    per-horizon breakdown, and the excluded-not-relabelled disposition.
  * JSON:    top-level "settlement_quarantine" with every count plus method,
    disposition and residual text.
  * per row: settlement_filtered (bool) and either settlement_excluded (count)
    or settlement_reason. false means UNCONFIRMED, not confirmed-absent — a
    snapshot cannot verify settlement, and must not read as if it had.

