REQUIRED AFTER APPLYING — this patch alone makes the grader REFUSE TO RUN
  require_registered_grader() compares self_sha256() against the newest chained
  grading-protocol record. Editing this file changes that digest, so against the
  live DB the grader will exit with "UNREGISTERED GRADER" until
  pipeline.PreregRegistrar appends a new AMENDMENT record re-pinning it (the
  12-hourly registrar pass, or a daemon restart — see
  proofs/P1_GRADER_AMENDMENT.md §9). That refusal is the governance working, not
  a defect in this patch; do not widen or bypass the check.

  Also unchanged by this patch, and deliberately so:
    * tools/make_repro_snapshot.py imports fetch_directional_days, so snapshots
      cut after this lands are cut from the FILTERED population. Re-cut the
      snapshot in the same change window as the re-pin.
    * measure_universe_completeness still measures over the UNFILTERED symbol
      set. It answers "is listing status resolvable", not "was this row graded",
      and narrowing it would change a survivorship figure this patch has no
      evidence to change.
    * the settlement guard itself is NOT deployed. This patch stops the grader
      publishing contaminated rows; it does not stop the resolver minting them.

